    {
      "bbox": [
        196,
        1864,
        1872,
        2755
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "In this connection, it should be noted that for periods of ordered military duty in excess of 30 days, Mil. Law § 245, which section applies to public employees who acquired a guard, militia or reserve status on or before April 1, 1942, provides that a city employee shall be paid the excess, if any, of his city over his military pay. Military Law § 43 which applies to public employees who acquired a guard, militia or reserve status after April 1, 1942, has no such provision for military differential - it merely provides for a continued leave of absence while the",
